{\large \textbf{Abstract}}\\
\begin{minipage}{0.9\textwidth}
The Aether-Metamorphosis-X (AMX) Kernel is a unified multi-physics engine
designed to transform astrophysical datasets, tensor-field manifolds, and
high-energy light-matter states under extreme conditions. The ST-99-ALPHA-EXT
configuration introduces dual-metric inversion capability, high-frequency
gravitational-wave strain processing, and peak energy-density metamorphosis
flux convergence. This manuscript presents the architecture, invariants,
execution pipeline, and stress-testing results of the AMX Kernel.
\end{minipage}\\[2em]

